<title>USA: Union Pacific names new chairman/CEO.</title>
<headline>Union Pacific names new chairman/CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BETHLEHEM, Pa. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Pacific Corp said on Thursday its board of directors elected Richard Davidson to succeed retiring chairman and chief executive officer Drew Lewis, 65, effective January 1, 1997.  </p>
<p>Davidson, 54, had been the company's president and chief operating officer for the past year and has worked in the railroad industry for 37 years, Union Pacific said.</p>
<p>The company said it was not looking to fill Davidson's two positions at this time, but declined to comment further.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
